{
  "description": "Mark catalog credentials the spec types as plain strings sensitive: BigQuery and GCS `credentialsKey` (the spec documents it as \"Base64 encoded or plain text BigQuery JSON key\" on BigQuery and \"Base64 encoded or plain text GCS JSON key\" on GCS, a Google service account key), Snowflake `privateKeyPassphrase` (\"Snowflake private key passphrase\") and the AstraDB connection's Cassandra `token` (\"AstraDB token\", the Astra application token that authenticates the connection). GCS and Cassandra catalogs are discriminated hierarchies, so their members sit on the per-arm structures convert flattens (`GcsCatalogGcsHiveMetastore`, `CreateCassandraCatalogRequestAstraDBConnection`, \u2026). Converter name patterns already mark the neighbouring `password`, `secretKey`, `glueSecretKey` and `privateKey` members; these three names fall outside them. Evidence: the field documentation in https://galaxy.starburst.io/public/openapi/v1/json (2026-11-11); no live call.",
